import marimo

__generated_with = "0.25.0"
app = marimo.App(width="medium")


@app.cell
def _(mo):
    _intro = mo.md(
        """
    # BAC Orbital Lifetime

    Estimates how long a CubeSat stays in orbit: a circular orbit decays under atmospheric drag until re-entry, with the atmosphere taken from NRLMSIS 2.1 and driven by the solar cycle. Drive it from the control panel or load a profile; profiles from the link budget, optical payload and power budget tools load their orbit here. The answer is an order of magnitude with a band, not a date: the same spacecraft lasts several times longer through a weak solar cycle than through a strong one.

    Compare the lifetime band against the planned mission and the disposal rules (5 years after end of mission for the FCC and ESA, 25 years for the IADC and ISO 24113), the altitude at end of mission that the siblings can evaluate at, and how much a deployable, a lighter build or a lower orbit moves the band.

    This tool lives at [bac.page/molab-orbital-lifetime](https://bac.page/molab-orbital-lifetime). Its siblings are the [link budget](https://bac.page/molab-link-budget), the [optical payload](https://bac.page/molab-optical-payload) and the [power budget](https://bac.page/molab-power-budget). The project is [buildacubesat.space](https://buildacubesat.space); source and issues are in [bac-utils](https://github.com/buildacubesat/bac-utils).
    """
    )
    _warn = mo.callout(
        mo.md(
            "Planning estimates only. The solar forecast, the drag coefficient and the attitude history dominate the result; treat the band as the answer and the single number as its center. Not a substitute for DAS, DRAMA or an operator's re-entry prediction."
        ),
        kind="warn",
    )
    mo.vstack([_intro, _warn])
    return


